Then I went back into Bandit:
- Level 3 done: I used ls with the a flag, found the hidden file "...Hiding-From-You", and got the password
- Level 4 done: I ran file ./ with a wildcard over all ten files, only file07 showed ASCII text, that was the password
- Level 5: in progress. I know I need find with type f and size 1033c. My first attempt gave no output because I ran it from the wrong directory. Tomorrow I will cd into inhere first and try again

Things I learned the hard way today:
- Filenames starting with a dash need ./ in front or the command thinks it is a flag
- file tells me what a file is, find searches for files. I mixed them up once
- When my network dropped, the SSH session closed and kicked me back home, but nothing was lost. Progress lives on their server, I just log back in and continue

Key takeaway: when a command gives no output or weird output, pwd tells me where I actually am, and that solves half the problem
